    {
      "hypothesis": "On the real BSE image, the lengthwise cutting of laths (median AR about 2.1) comes mainly from the distance-transform watershed with the low h_px=0.5 and from too-short along-axis bridging (bridge_gaps_px=9). If so, raising h_px to about 1.5 and bridge_gaps_px to 12 should raise the median AR in the lower fine band and reduce grey fragments. If AR stays near 2 and the upper-half merging is unchanged, the beta ribs are at or below what this ridge filter resolves, and parameter tuning cannot fix it.",
      "rationale": "Confidence is low, about 30%, that this alone makes the drawing acceptable. The twin is untrusted (boundary width ratio 1.8, coherence ratio 0.72), so no search runs and only a few changes are made, each tied to what the reviewers saw. Both reviews accept the boundary reading: dark alpha laths between thin bright beta ribs. Polarity bright_boundaries therefore stays. The reviewers named three failures, and each change targets one of them. (1) Laths cut along their length (AR about 2.1, lower third broken into stubs). For this, h_px goes from 0.5 to 1.5 so the watershed splits only clearly necked regions, and bridge_gaps_px goes from 9 to 12; the bridging closes only along the lath direction, so it should not bridge across laths. (2) Many small fragments counted or greyed. For this, min_area_px goes from 30 to 50, in line with the reviewer's suggestion of about 40. (3) Over-merging of parallel laths in the upper half. For this, boundary_sensitivity goes from 0.8 to 0.7 so fainter ribs are kept as boundaries. This pulls against (1), which the larger h_px and bridging are meant to offset. Not changed: boundary_width_px stays at 2.0, since the reviewer asks for a smaller ridge scale and 2.0 is already small. The scratch params also stay: the second review says the white line at x=1175 is the mean-direction arrow, so the false scratch is not established. The rotation check (0.45 before) must be re-run, and none of the measured numbers is supported until a review accepts the drawing. The search space is listed for when a better twin is built; it is not run now.",
